<body lang=EN-IN style='tab-interval:36.0pt;word-wrap:break-word'>

<div class=WordSection1>

<div>

<p class=MsoNormal><b><span style='font-size:20.0pt'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span></span></b><b><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif;
color:#EE0000'>Customer Segmentation using K-means Clustering<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:
"Baskerville Old Face",serif;color:#0070C0'>Project Overview<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Narrow",sans-serif'>Customer
segmentation is a crucial technique used by businesses to divide customers into
distinct groups based on their characteristics and behavior. This project
focuses on applying the K-Means clustering algorithm to segment customers based
on their demographic and spending patterns.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Narrow",sans-serif'>The
primary objective of this project is to identify meaningful customer groups
that can help businesses design targeted marketing strategies, improve customer
satisfaction, and maximize profitability. By leveraging unsupervised machine
learning techniques, we aim to uncover hidden patterns in customer data without
predefined labels.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Narrow",sans-serif'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span><span style='color:#0070C0'>Dataset Summary</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>The
dataset used in this project contains customer-related information such as:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l5 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><span
     style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Customer
     ID<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l5 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><span
     style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Gender<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l5 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><span
     style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Age<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l5 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><span
     style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Annual
     Income (k$)<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l5 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><span
     style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Spending
     Score (1&#8211;100)<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Among
these, the most important features used for clustering are:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<ul style='margin-top:0cm' type=disc>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l3 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Annual
     Income (k$)</span></b><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'><o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l3 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>Spending
     Score (1&#8211;100)</span></b><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:
     "Aptos Display",sans-serif'><o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'>These
features help in understanding customer purchasing behavior and financial
capacity. The dataset was checked for missing values and cleaned accordingly to
ensure accurate analysis.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span><span style='color:#0070C0'>Exploratory
Data Analysis using Python<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-themecolor:text1'>Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) was performed
to understand the distribution and relationships within the dataset. Various
visualization techniques were used:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-themecolor:text1'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif;
color:#0070C0'>Distribution Analysis<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-themecolor:text1'>-<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Count plots were used to analyze gender distribution.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Aptos Display",sans-serif;
color:black;mso-themecolor:text1'>-<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;
</span>Histograms were used to understand age distribution.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:20.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif;
color:black;mso-themecolor:text1'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:16.0pt;font-family:"Baskerville Old Face",serif;
